EN

## 1. Public repository

This repository is public and contains official releases of Cubic Battle 4
only: APK files, EXE files, archives, checksums, release notes, and related
files.

Public access means that anyone may download officially published releases free
of charge. It does not mean that the source code is published or that any
rights to the source code are granted.

## 2. Permitted use

The rights holder grants each user a free, non-exclusive, non-transferable
right to:

- download an official release from this repository;
- install and run Cubic Battle 4 on their own devices;
- create screenshots, gameplay recordings, streams, reviews, and other user
  content featuring the game;
- publish and monetise videos, streams, clips, podcasts, and other audiovisual
  publications featuring the game, its music, or its sounds.

Usual technical edits for audiovisual publications are allowed, including
trimming, volume changes, fades, synchronisation with video, and commentary.
Credit is appreciated but not required.

## 3. Music and sounds

Original music and sounds included in an official release may be used in
videos, streams, clips, podcasts, and other audiovisual publications,
including monetised publications.

Without the prior written permission of the rights holder, you may not:

- distribute the audio files on their own;
- sell or license the music as a standalone music catalogue;
- include the music or sounds in another game, app, bundle, mod, or sound
  library;
- create remixes, covers, or other musical derivative works;
- claim authorship of the music, sounds, or other game materials.

## 4. Restrictions

Without the prior written permission of the rights holder, you may not:

- republish, repackage, sell, or distribute game releases as your own;
- modify release files or add advertising, malware, cheats, or mods;
- decompile, disassemble, extract source code, or bypass technical protections,
  except where applicable law expressly permits it;
- use the game name, logos, characters, artwork, or other materials to create
  your own product or mislead users;
- remove copyright notices, checksums, or attribution;
- claim the game, its materials, or official releases as your own.

Use of the game does not grant rights to the source code, trademarks,
characters, artwork, server infrastructure, or other materials except where
expressly stated in this license.

## 5. Third-party components

Third-party components included in a release retain their own licenses. Their
terms prevail over this license for the relevant component.

## 6. No warranty

The game and releases are provided “as is”, without warranty of any kind. The
rights holder does not guarantee uninterrupted operation, compatibility with
all devices, progress preservation, or continued availability of online
features.

## 7. Termination

Any breach of this license automatically terminates the granted permission.
After termination, the user must delete their copies of the release unless
applicable law requires otherwise.
